            <ArticleTitle>Effect of weight on indwelling catheter use among long-term care facility residents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>194-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study examined the effect of obesity on the use of indwelling urinary catheters among long-term care facility residents and found initial increases in usage by weight category, which declined during the next 12 months.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
